1 _CONFLEVEL primary
1 NOTE A tin miner from St Just. He married Elizabeth Ann Trembath at Penzance in 1866. They sailed for America in 1868 and settled at Mineral Point, where he worked in the lead and zinc mines for more than thirty years.
1 NOTE The 1904 county album says he came to America in 1867. The 1868 passenger list and his 1912 obituary both give 1868. The album was compiled long after the event, so the register uses 1868.
1 NOTE [TODO] His baptism names his parents as Richard and Grace Penhallow of Trewellard. Enter them once a second record confirms the family.
1 NOTE [NEGATIVE] 2026-10-12 — Searched the sample St Just burial register for 1845–1868 for Richard Penhallow; not found. He may have died after John emigrated.
1 FAMS @F0001@
